  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Pleasant/dry pattern with comfortably low \ndaytime humidity continues into the last weekend of July \n\nCloud cover will increase into tonight, but no rain is expected.\nDry weather continues for the majority of CPA through Saturday \nwith just a low chance of an isolated shower/t-storm along the \nwestern periphery of the Allegheny Mtns during the afternoon\npeak heating cycle. We adjusted dewpoints lower for Saturday \nafternoon over east central PA based on the hires model signal.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Turning more humid and unsettled into early next\nweek with the best odds for storms Monday PM through Tuesday PM\n\nShortwave energy diving southeast around the prominent upper\nhigh centered over central and southern Plains will help to \neventually carve out a closed upper low over the eastern Great\nLakes by early next week. Expect a gradual increase in shower\nand thunderstorm coverage Sunday through Tuesday with peak POPs\nin the Monday PM-Tuesday PM window based on the latest ensemble\nguidance. There will likely be some level of severe and/or\nexcessive rain risks to manage that are largely dependent on\ntiming/upstream system evolution at this point.",
